# Cliffhangers. A `hook` is the last line of its flight day; its resolver (`due`,
# `when fired <hook>`) opens the next day. The engine spaces hooks >= 4 days apart.
# Resolutions: mostly satisfying, sometimes ominous, never "it was nothing".
# All hooks share hook_who to carry the astronaut over; they never overlap.
# House style: content/STYLE.md.

# --- 1. Emergency band ---------------------------------------------------------
card h_band
type event
cat mystery
hook
once
days 25 38
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text At 23:40 the dish on {A}'s ship logs a burst on the emergency band. The bearing is Mars.

card r_band
type event
cat mystery
clue
due
once
days 26 42
roles A
when fired h_band
when is A hook_who
text {A} decodes it by breakfast: a lander's safe-mode beacon, asking for instructions nobody sent. The header format is old. {A} matches it to a science lander that went quiet years ago, logs it, and is almost sure.
do trait A curious 3
do morale A 4

# --- 2. Cabin pressure -------------------------------------------------------
card h_pressure
type event
cat repair
hook
once
days 4 40
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text 01:50. The cabin pressure on {A}'s ship has started to fall. Slowly. {A} is the only one awake.

card r_pressure
type event
cat repair
due
once
days 5 42
roles A
when fired h_pressure
when is A hook_who
text {A} spent four hours with an ultrasonic leak detector and a roll of tape. The culprit was a cable feedthrough whose seal shrank in the cold of the shaded side. It's resealed, the pressure holds, and the trend line is pinned to the wall like a trophy.
do res spares -1
do morale A 5

# --- 3. Solar flare ----------------------------------------------------------
card h_flare
type event
cat grim
hook
once
days 4 40
weight 9
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text 23:52. The space weather feed flags a major flare on the Sun. Protons will reach the fleet in about forty minutes. {A} starts waking people up.

card r_flare
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 5 42
roles A
when fired h_flare
when is A hook_who
text Every crew spent the night in the storm shelter between the water tanks, shoulder to shoulder, listening to the dosimeters tick. By morning the fleet had taken a month's dose in six hours, and everyone walked out on their own feet. {A} logged the peak and went to make coffee.
do var storms 1
do morale A 3

# --- 4. Uncommanded thruster --------------------------------------------------
card h_thruster
type event
cat repair skill
hook
once
days 4 40
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text 02:14. A thruster on {A}'s ship fires without a command. Then another. {A} is already at the console.

card r_thruster
type event
cat repair skill
due
once
days 5 42
roles A
when fired h_thruster
when is A hook_who
lean brave manual watch
text By 02:30 the ship was steady again.
option manual | Hand control | {A} took attitude into manual, just for a minute, and held it by hand while the valve telemetry scrolled past. One valve reported "closed" while it leaked. It's isolated now, and the log of the night is a single calm page.
  trait A brave 2
  morale A 4
option watch | Isolate and watch | {A} let the control loop fight it and watched the pulses, counting. Every one traced to a single valve that reported "closed" while it leaked. It's isolated now, and the plot of the night is pinned up with the leak circled in red.
  trait A curious 2
  morale A 4

# --- 5. Alarm flood -----------------------------------------------------------
card h_flood
type event
cat repair skill
hook
once
days 4 40
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text Just before midnight, 214 alarms hit {A}'s console at once. One of them is real.

card r_flood
type event
cat repair skill
due
once
days 5 42
roles A
when fired h_flood
when is A hook_who
text {A} found it at 01:30, buried on page nine: a coolant pump drawing too much current, minutes from tripping. {A} swapped to the backup before the primary died. By morning the alarm list had been cut from 214 to 11, and nobody is sure when {A} slept.
do morale A 5
do res spares -1

# --- 6. Ground silence --------------------------------------------------------
card h_silence
type event
cat grim
hook
once
days 10 40
weight 8
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text Mission Control misses a scheduled check-in. Then the next one. {A} sends a third hail and starts the clock: forty minutes for an answer.

card r_silence
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 11 42
roles A
when fired h_silence
when is A hook_who
text The reply arrived at 06:12. A ground station had gone down in a storm at home, and the backup took all night to come up. The message ends: "All good here. How are you?" {A} reads it twice before answering.
do morale A 6
do trait A warm 2

# --- 7. Hull strike -----------------------------------------------------------
card h_strike
type event
cat grim
hook
once
days 4 40
weight 9
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text Something hits {A}'s ship hard enough to ring the hull like a bell. Every pressure reading is green. {A} doesn't trust green.

card r_strike
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 5 42
roles A
when fired h_strike
when is A hook_who
text The morning EVA found a crater the size of a fingernail in a shield panel, and behind it, nothing. The shielding did its job. {A} photographed it next to a ruler, and the anomaly report finally has a good picture.
do trait A brave 2
do morale A 3

# --- 8. Star tracker ghost (ominous) ---------------------------------------------
card h_ghost
type event
cat mystery
hook
once
days 25 38
weight 8
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text {A}'s star tracker flags a catalog mismatch: one star too many in the field. On the next frame, it has moved.

card r_ghost
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 26 42
roles A
when fired h_ghost
when is A hook_who
text {A} pinned it down by morning: a spent upper stage from a Mars mission decades ago, tumbling along almost the same path. It will pass forty kilometers off the bow. It has been out here the whole time, and no one is coming for it.
do trait A curious 3
do morale A -2


# --- 9. A voice on the loop ----------------------------------------------------------
card h_voice
type event
cat mystery
hook
once
days 25 36
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text 02:40. The intercom on {A}'s ship opens by itself. A voice says {A}'s name, once, softly. Everyone else aboard is asleep.

card r_voice
type event
cat human
due
once
days 26 42
roles A
when fired h_voice
when is A hook_who
text {A} traced it by dawn: a message from home, recorded the night before launch, set to play on this flight day and then buried under a software update. The rest of it plays at breakfast. {A} listens with the volume very low.
do morale A 6
do trait A warm 3

# --- 10. A ship drops off the net -------------------------------------------------
card h_dark
type event
cat mystery
hook
once
days 27 38
weight 8
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text 23:58. {A}'s ship drops off the fleet net in the middle of a sentence. No beacon, no telemetry, just an empty slot on six displays.

card r_dark
type event
cat mystery
clue
due
once
days 28 42
roles A
when fired h_dark
when is A hook_who
text {A}'s voice came back at 05:40, steady. The main antenna had slewed toward Mars on a command with a valid fleet signature, sent from no ship in the fleet. Mission Control says it is looking into it. It has said that before.
do trait A brave 3
do morale A -2
